---
interface Props { title?: string }
const { title = 'Working values and saved files' } = Astro.props;
const levels = [
  { name: 'CPU registers', detail: 'Values named directly by instructions', size: 'Smallest working set', width: '64%', role: 'flow' },
  { name: 'CPU caches · L1 / L2 / L3', detail: 'Copies of memory lines near the CPU', size: 'A hit avoids a slower fetch', width: '78%', role: 'data' },
  { name: 'Main memory · RAM', detail: 'Resident program code and data', size: 'A larger working set', width: '92%', role: 'data' },
];
---
<figure class="hierarchy-diagram" aria-label={title}>
  <figcaption><strong>{title}</strong><span>Working storage above · persistent storage below</span></figcaption>
  <ol class="hierarchy-diagram__levels" aria-label="Memory hierarchy">
    {levels.map(level => <li style={`--level-width:${level.width}`} data-memory-role={level.role}>
      <strong>{level.name}</strong><span>{level.detail}</span><small>{level.size}</small>
    </li>)}
  </ol>
  <div class="hierarchy-diagram__boundary"><span aria-hidden="true">↕</span><strong>Explicit file I/O or OS paging</strong><span>Storage access is a separate operation</span></div>
  <div class="hierarchy-diagram__storage" role="group" aria-label="Persistent storage">
    <section><svg viewBox="0 0 32 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="3" width="28" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M7 8h18M7 12h18M7 16h8"/></svg><strong>SSD</strong><span>Persistent files in flash storage</span></section>
    <section><svg viewBox="0 0 32 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="2" width="28" height="20" rx="2"/><circle cx="15" cy="12" r="7"/><circle cx="15" cy="12" r="2"/><path d="m17 12 9 5"/></svg><strong>HDD</strong><span>Persistent files on magnetic disks</span></section>
  </div>
  <p>A cache miss can require a RAM fetch; it does not automatically mean a disk read. Capacity and timing depend on the machine.</p>
</figure>
<style>
.hierarchy-diagram { --hierarchy-data: var(--semantic-data, var(--chapter-accent)); --hierarchy-flow: var(--semantic-flow, var(--chapter-accent)); margin-block: 1.5rem; padding: 1.25rem; color: var(--ink); background: var(--paper); border: .0625rem solid var(--line); border-radius: .75rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram figcaption { display: grid; gap: .25rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram figcaption strong { font-size: 1.1rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram figcaption span, .hierarchy-diagram small { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .85rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram__levels { display: grid; gap: .5rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
.hierarchy-diagram__levels li { position: relative; display: grid; justify-items: center; gap: .25rem; width: var(--level-width); min-width: 12rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; text-align: center; isolation: isolate; }
.hierarchy-diagram__levels li::before { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -1; content: ''; clip-path: polygon(6% 0,94% 0,100% 100%,0 100%); background: color-mix(in oklch,var(--hierarchy-data) 7%,var(--paper)); }
.hierarchy-diagram__levels li[data-memory-role="flow"]::before { background: color-mix(in oklch,var(--hierarchy-flow) 7%,var(--paper)); }
.hierarchy-diagram__levels strong { color: var(--hierarchy-data); font-size: 1rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram__levels [data-memory-role="flow"] strong { color: var(--hierarchy-flow); }
.hierarchy-diagram__levels span { font-size: .9rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram__boundary { display: grid; justify-items: center; gap: .25rem; margin-block: 1rem; text-align: center; }
.hierarchy-diagram__boundary > span:first-child { color: var(--hierarchy-flow); font-size: 1.8rem; line-height: 1; }
.hierarchy-diagram__boundary > span:last-child { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.hierarchy-diagram__storage { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: .75rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram__storage section { display: grid; justify-items: center; gap: .25rem; padding: .75rem; background: color-mix(in oklch,var(--hierarchy-data) 5%,var(--paper)); border: .0625rem solid var(--line); border-radius: .5rem; text-align: center; }
.hierarchy-diagram__storage svg { width: 2.75rem; height: 2.25rem; fill: none; stroke: var(--hierarchy-data); stroke-width: 1.5; }
.hierarchy-diagram__storage span { font-size: .9rem; }
.hierarchy-diagram p { margin: 1rem 0 0; font-size: .9rem; }
:global(html[data-academy-semantic="off"]) .hierarchy-diagram { --hierarchy-data: var(--ink); --hierarchy-flow: var(--ink); }
@media (max-width: 30rem) { .hierarchy-diagram { padding: .75rem; } .hierarchy-diagram__levels li { min-width: 0; width: max(var(--level-width),75%); padding: .85rem .75rem; } }
@media print { .hierarchy-diagram { break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>
